PURPOSE of /kernel/power-management/rapl/multithread_load
Description: Test if perf (via RAPL) is reporting bigger power consumption for bigger loads.
Author: Erik Hamera <ehamera@redhat.com>

RAPL = Running Average Power Limit

Check RAPL functions. It works with assumption, that under heavier load the CPU shouldn't
consume less power (in some error range). The error range is 20% now - it is __NOT__
wisely choosen magical number emerging from intel's datasheets or something like that.
It __IS__ just wild guess which should suppress false alarms due to started daemons and
other fluctuations. Feel free to change it if your guess is better, than mine.

It works on RHEL 7. There is no appropriate event in perf on RHEL 6, so porting would
be very hard, or impossible.

